    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Four cuts",
      "href": "#overview",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Split order",
      "href": "#split-plan",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "CLI dispatcher",
      "href": "#C1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "01 clock",
      "href": "#unit-1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "02 authority",
      "href": "#unit-2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "03 · copy and organize ↓",
      "href": "#unit-3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "04\nDaemonClient\nexecute · control",
      "href": "#unit-4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Private mechanism owners\nrouting · process · registry · delivery · workers …",
      "href": "#unit-3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "process-entry / worker-entry",
      "href": "#C2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Own time\n↗",
      "href": "#unit-1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "A1\nDaemon owns wall/monotonic time; the standalone queue default changes Date.now → monotonic, while the process already injected monotonic time.",
      "href": "#A1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "A2\nIdle still starts at construction and resets at acceptance; readiness and completion resets are deferred.",
      "href": "#A2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Own process authority\n↗",
      "href": "#unit-2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "B1\nThe registry owns startup equality, with narrow credentials and full observed-owner checks.",
      "href": "#B1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "B2\nThe process coordinator validates and adopts launch coordinates before composing its internals.",
      "href": "#B2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "B3\nWorkspaceDaemon becomes DaemonProcessCoordinator; narrow ports replace generic dependency options.",
      "href": "#B3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "B4\nRequest authentication order is characterized and retained, including the identity/termination exceptions.",
      "href": "#B4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Stage a package\n↗",
      "href": "#unit-3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C1\nStage package mechanisms while the live CLI keeps 38 frozen local files; the hash normalizes CRLF.",
      "href": "#C1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C2\nOrganize private mechanism owners and expose package-relative process and worker executables.",
      "href": "#C2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C3\n37 mechanism tests move to the package and use package-independent executor fixtures.",
      "href": "#C3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C4\nA new raw-clock guard narrows to lifecycle/ during staging; the PR base had no such guard.",
      "href": "#C4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C5\nThe mocked CLI entry test is deleted; built package entries gain execution and platform-specific cleanup tests.",
      "href": "#C5",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C6\nThe temporary policy-testing export, its import restriction and two lint tests are retired together.",
      "href": "#C6",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C7\nPackage test files run serially; the fixture environment adds tsx and local test helpers.",
      "href": "#C7",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "C8\nCLI worker timing and mismatch-initialization assertions are removed; direct executor version rejection is restored.",
      "href": "#C8",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Give hosts a client\n↗",
      "href": "#unit-4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D1\nA Node-free public facade loads a Node runtime at construction; only execute/control cross the new host boundary.",
      "href": "#D1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D2\nOrdered lazy guards stop later observations: disabled → record → starting → version → responsiveness.",
      "href": "#D2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D3\nAbsent/dead/incompatible routes trigger independent startup; local attempts get a fresh executor and keep their chosen mode.",
      "href": "#D3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D4\nWarm failures retry locally only when transport marks them safe; uncertain/accepted failures return controlled output.",
      "href": "#D4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D5\nThe client owns warm output capture in the OS temp directory, failure bytes and malformed-output cleanup.",
      "href": "#D5",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D6\nControl has typed start/status/stop results, a separate status timeout, disabled-start short circuit and propagated errors.",
      "href": "#D6",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "D7\nThe host supplies readiness command/argv through startup, preserving the queued executor probe.",
      "href": "#D7",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "↑ Four cuts",
      "href": "#overview",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "id": "",
      "text": "A1\nDaemon wall and monotonic clocks replace telemetry and scattered time callbacks.\nSTATED",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
